  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Utah received $96.6M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Utah recorded 417 awards, with an average award size of $232K. Obligations fell 98.6% year over year. Historical totals show large prior-year activity: FY22 totaled $5.3B, FY23 totaled $6.4B, FY24 totaled $7.3B, FY25 totaled $5.3B, and FY26 totaled $7.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $42.4M in Utah this fiscal year to date, followed by the Department of Housing and Urban Development with $27.2M and the Department of the Interior with $12.9M. ALPINE COMPANIES, INC. received $27.2M, BIOMERIEUX INC received $21.1M, and GIDEON CONTRACTING, LIMITED LIABILITY COMPANY received $9M. Residential Property Managers accounted for $27.2M, In-Vitro Diagnostic Substance Manufacturing accounted for $19.5M, and Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction accounted for $9M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
