        "heading": "How much federal contract spending has Utah seen this fiscal year to date?",
        "body": "Utah received $96.6M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Utah recorded 417 awards with an average award size of $232K. Utah obligations fell 98.6% year over year. Prior fiscal years show much larger totals: FY26 was $7.1B, FY25 was $5.3B, FY24 was $7.3B, FY23 was $6.4B, and FY22 was $5.3B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries are the largest buyers and performers in Utah right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $42.4M, followed by the Department of Housing and Urban Development with $27.2M and the Department of the Interior with $12.9M. ALPINE COMPANIES, INC. is the top vendor with $27.2M, BIOMERIEUX INC is second with $21.1M, and GIDEON CONTRACTING, LIMITED LIABILITY COMPANY is third with $9M. Residential Property Managers lead industry spending with $27.2M, In-Vitro Diagnostic Substance Manufacturing follows with $19.5M, and Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction accounts for $9M."
